# Promise.resolve(Symbol.iterator).then(Math.abs).catch(handler);  Promise.resolve(converted).then(Math.floor).catch(other);  function handler(caught) { return caught }
# The row of Math.abs declares no throw: that covers the function once its operand is a number. The conversion of a symbol throws a TypeError, so the promise that `then` answers may be
# rejected with an object that native code makes, and the handler is not proven to get undefined. A conversion also runs code of the operand, which throws any value.
# RUN: valueflow-apply
# CHECK: function f1 name="handler" {{*}}parameters=[{type=anything}]
# CHECK: function f2 name="other" {{*}}parameters=[{type=anything}]

